, "overview": "New Hampshire's open Senate seat pits Representative Chris Pappas against former Senator John Sununu, with Jeanne Shaheen retiring. Pappas has led every high-quality poll since early September, typically by five to eight points, and recent surveys from Saint Anselm and YouGov reinforce that picture. Ratings from Cook, NBC, and others cluster at Lean or Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price Pappas around ninety percent.\n\nPappas holds a substantial fundraising advantage, though Sununu benefits from outside spending and strong name recognition in a state his family has long dominated. The race remains closer than the national environment alone would suggest, but the weight of polling, money, and expert judgment points to a Pappas win with modest but real uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8721, "margin": 5.76}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8221, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7959, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8661, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8028, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.837, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8746, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8609, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.856, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8659, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8767, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8474, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8665, "margin": 5.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.841, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8206, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8623, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.8967, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.8462, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.8579, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.8632, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.8916, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "